WEBVTT

00:00:07.904 --> 00:00:11.947
Mystery in San Francisco by Gina D.B.

00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:16.330
Clement.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:25.385
Copyright Blackcat Publishing.

00:00:25.445 --> 00:00:33.664
Introduction.

00:00:33.724 --> 00:00:39.389
The story you are going to read takes place in San Francisco, California.

00:00:39.449 --> 00:00:43.910
San Francisco is a beautiful city on the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.571
It is on a peninsula.

00:00:46.631 --> 00:00:51.212
San Francisco is on the San Andreas fault line.

00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:55.973
This means that sometimes there are earthquakes in San Francisco.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:01.358
A big earthquake in 1906 almost destroyed the city.

00:01:01.418 --> 00:01:06.125
The last serious earthquake was in 1989.

00:01:06.185 --> 00:01:10.869
It doesn't rain much and it is often foggy.

00:01:10.928 --> 00:01:16.332
You can see the fog arrive under the Golden Gate Bridge in the late afternoon.

00:01:16.392 --> 00:01:21.026
It stays all night and then it leaves late in the morning.

00:01:21.086 --> 00:01:24.258
At night you can hear fog horns.

00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:29.139
They warn ships on the ocean about dangerous weather conditions.

00:01:29.199 --> 00:01:39.344
The city has beautiful scenery because there are many hills, a lot of vegetation and attractive buildings.

00:01:39.404 --> 00:01:51.944
The North Beach Neighborhood North Beach is a traditionally Italian neighborhood with Italian food shops, cafes and restaurants.

00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:57.003
North Beach was one of the first settlements because it was near the bay.

00:01:57.063 --> 00:02:06.110
In the 1950s, many of the beach generation, a group of artists, writers and poets lived in North Beach.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:11.100
City Lights Bookstore was the center for these writers and poets.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.891
Today, you can still visit this bookstore.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:21.792
During the Gold Rush, Telegraph Hill was very important because it had a view of the bay.

00:02:21.852 --> 00:02:26.354
People on Telegraph Hill looked for sailing ships on the bay.

00:02:26.414 --> 00:02:32.708
When a sailing ship arrived, a messenger from Telegraph Hill went to tell the people.

00:02:32.768 --> 00:02:36.241
Today, there is a big tower on the hill.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.073
It is called Coit Tower.

00:02:39.132 --> 00:02:46.888
A woman called Lily Hitchcock Coit, built it in honor of the firefighters of San Francisco.

00:02:46.948 --> 00:02:53.502
Washington Square is a lovely park and meeting place for the people of North Beach.

00:02:53.562 --> 00:03:01.410
Often, there are arts festivals in the square.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:22.288
In Chapter 1, Washington Square Jim Riley was 14 years old, and he lived in the beautiful city of San Francisco in California.

00:03:22.348 --> 00:03:25.330
He was short, thin, and wore glasses.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.942
He had brown hair and blue eyes.

00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:33.716
His mother died when he was 6 years old, and his father lived in another city.

00:03:33.776 --> 00:03:36.287
Jim lived with his grandfather.

00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:40.769
This was his first year in high school and he liked it a lot.

00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:43.510
His favorite subject was science.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:49.144
On weekends he had a part-time job at a supermarket to make extra pocket money.

00:03:49.204 --> 00:03:54.167
Jim's home was on Telegraph Hill near San Francisco Bay.

00:03:54.227 --> 00:03:58.970
From his living room he could see the Golden Gate Bridge and the Bay.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.338
Every morning he walked down Telegraph Hill.

00:04:02.398 --> 00:04:06.088
He met his friends at the bus stop at Washington Square.

00:04:06.147 --> 00:04:08.910
They went to high school together.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:16.445
Washington Square was a historical landmark, and the people of San Francisco loved to go there.

00:04:16.505 --> 00:04:19.888
It was a lovely park for children and adults.

00:04:19.948 --> 00:04:22.620
It was a small playground for children.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.833
It was also a place for the people of the North Beach neighborhood to meet.

00:04:26.893 --> 00:04:32.108
There were restaurants, cafes, and nice shops around Washington Square.

00:04:32.168 --> 00:04:35.152
Often there were music and arts festivals.

00:04:35.212 --> 00:04:49.299
Normally, Washington Square had green grass and beautiful flowers, but there was no rain for a long time and the grass was dry and yellow and the flowers were dead.

00:04:49.359 --> 00:04:53.717
Brian Wilson was Jim's best friend.

00:04:53.777 --> 00:04:55.518
He was 14, too.

00:04:55.578 --> 00:04:59.932
He was a tall boy with blonde curly hair and green eyes.

00:04:59.992 --> 00:05:02.994
He played basketball on the high school team.

00:05:03.054 --> 00:05:07.368
His parents had a grocery store, and he helped them on weekends.

00:05:07.428 --> 00:05:08.849
Hi, Brian.

00:05:08.909 --> 00:05:10.830
Did you finish your English homework?

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.172
Said Jim.

00:05:12.232 --> 00:05:13.623
Yes, I did.

00:05:13.683 --> 00:05:15.655
But Shakespeare wasn't easy.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.466
Look, there's Susan.

00:05:17.526 --> 00:05:18.767
Said Brian.

00:05:18.827 --> 00:05:19.980
Hi, guys.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.404
said Susan.

00:05:21.464 --> 00:05:25.146
Susan Hardy was a pretty African-American girl.

00:05:25.206 --> 00:05:27.628
She was a good friend of both boys.

00:05:27.688 --> 00:05:30.239
She was also a very good student.

00:05:30.299 --> 00:05:36.252
She had a part-time job as a babysitter for the children of her neighbors, the Moreno family.

00:05:36.312 --> 00:05:39.064
Her brother Tom was 20 years old.

00:05:39.124 --> 00:05:45.788
He was a biology student at San Francisco University and played on the university football team.

00:05:45.848 --> 00:05:48.330
Are you ready for the math test?

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.736
Ask Susan.

00:05:49.796 --> 00:05:53.262
I studied all afternoon yesterday, but I'm not ready.

00:05:53.322 --> 00:05:54.552
Said Brian.

00:05:54.612 --> 00:05:56.012
I'm not either.

00:05:56.072 --> 00:05:57.853
I didn't look at my notes.

00:05:57.913 --> 00:05:59.404
Said Jim.

00:05:59.463 --> 00:06:02.484
The bus came, and they got on.

00:06:02.544 --> 00:06:05.765
They saw their school friends and started talking.

00:06:05.825 --> 00:06:09.939
The bus was always crowded, but the bus ride was fun.

00:06:09.998 --> 00:06:16.506
When they got near Galileo High School, they could smell the chocolate from the chocolate factory nearby.

00:06:16.566 --> 00:06:19.029
They loved the smell of the chocolate.

00:06:19.089 --> 00:06:21.471
It made them hungry.

00:06:21.531 --> 00:06:24.584
The math test was difficult.

00:06:24.644 --> 00:06:28.118
The students were happy when it was finally lunchtime.

00:06:28.178 --> 00:06:31.227
They all went to the big school cafeteria.

00:06:31.286 --> 00:06:34.536
Why is math so difficult, said Jim?

00:06:34.596 --> 00:06:37.438
I think Mrs. Miller makes the test difficult.

00:06:37.498 --> 00:06:41.432
Don't worry about the test and eat your lunch, said Brian.

00:06:41.492 --> 00:06:45.105
In the afternoon, they had a long science lesson.

00:06:45.165 --> 00:06:46.876
It was very interesting.

00:06:46.936 --> 00:06:50.480
They studied chemistry in the school laboratory.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.734
They often did experiments with their chemistry teacher, Mr. Woods.

00:06:54.794 --> 00:06:56.898
They liked Mr. Woods.

00:06:56.958 --> 00:07:00.702
At a quarter past three, the school bell rang.

00:07:00.762 --> 00:07:03.495
It was time to go home and it was Friday.

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:05.216
What are you doing this weekend?

00:07:05.276 --> 00:07:06.378
Ask Brian.

00:07:06.438 --> 00:07:08.719
I'm working at the supermarket tomorrow.

00:07:08.779 --> 00:07:09.600
Said Jim.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.732
But on Sunday, I'm coming to see your basketball game.

00:07:12.792 --> 00:07:13.994
I hope we win.

00:07:14.054 --> 00:07:15.254
Said Brian.

00:07:15.314 --> 00:07:18.458
I'm working tomorrow as well at my parents' grocery store.

00:07:18.518 --> 00:07:21.556
It's always a busy day, but I'm free tomorrow night.

00:07:21.616 --> 00:07:25.655
Well, I'm babysitting for the Moreno children all weekend.

00:07:25.715 --> 00:07:26.826
Said Susan.

00:07:26.886 --> 00:07:29.187
Do you want to go to the movies tomorrow night, Jim?

00:07:29.247 --> 00:07:30.357
Ask Brian.

00:07:30.417 --> 00:07:33.409
Yes, that's a great idea, said Jim.

00:07:33.469 --> 00:07:40.792
I'll phone you.

00:07:40.852 --> 00:07:48.286
Chapter 2.

00:07:48.346 --> 00:07:58.723
The Face at the Window Jim walked slowly up Telegraph Hill.

00:07:58.783 --> 00:08:01.824
It was a foggy afternoon in February.

00:08:01.884 --> 00:08:05.515
Every day, Jim walked in front of an old mansion.

00:08:05.575 --> 00:08:10.956
It was a mysterious wooden building with a big garden and a fence around it.

00:08:11.016 --> 00:08:15.628
Jim often looked at it and thought, what's inside?

00:08:15.688 --> 00:08:18.059
Why doesn't anyone live here?

00:08:18.119 --> 00:08:21.640
That afternoon, he stopped in front of the gate.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.658
He looked at the garden and the trees.

00:08:24.718 --> 00:08:26.864
What a strange place.

00:08:26.924 --> 00:08:28.805
No one took care of it.

00:08:28.865 --> 00:08:31.435
Then he looked up at the old mansion.

00:08:31.495 --> 00:08:34.366
He looked at the window on the second floor.

00:08:34.426 --> 00:08:36.446
There was a face behind it.

00:08:36.506 --> 00:08:38.216
He felt cold.

00:08:38.276 --> 00:08:42.737
It was the face of a little girl with long dark hair.

00:08:42.797 --> 00:08:45.478
But no one lived in that mansion.

00:08:45.538 --> 00:08:47.138
Who was it?

00:08:47.198 --> 00:08:48.928
A ghost?

00:08:48.988 --> 00:08:51.578
Jim didn't believe in ghosts.

00:08:51.638 --> 00:08:54.174
But who was the girl at the window?

00:08:54.234 --> 00:08:56.240
She looked down at him.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.752
He continued looking at the window.

00:08:58.812 --> 00:09:02.404
Suddenly the face of the girl disappeared.

00:09:02.464 --> 00:09:06.198
Jim could not see well because it was very foggy.

00:09:06.257 --> 00:09:08.860
He decided to go home quickly.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:12.132
He walked in the door and into the living room.

00:09:12.192 --> 00:09:15.516
He saw his grandfather in the corner of the room.

00:09:15.576 --> 00:09:19.659
Grandpa, he cried, I saw a ghost.

00:09:19.719 --> 00:09:21.180
What did you say?

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.376
asked his grandfather with a smile.

00:09:23.436 --> 00:09:27.352
I saw the face of a little girl at the window of the old mansion.

00:09:27.412 --> 00:09:30.062
No one lives there, but I saw a girl.

00:09:30.123 --> 00:09:31.443
She looked at me.

00:09:31.503 --> 00:09:33.784
Are you sure, Jim?

00:09:33.844 --> 00:09:36.994
It's a very foggy afternoon.

00:09:37.054 --> 00:09:40.005
Did you see her clearly?

00:09:40.065 --> 00:09:43.416
No one lives in the old steward mansion.

00:09:43.476 --> 00:09:46.426
It's about 100 years old.

00:09:46.486 --> 00:09:52.638
There's a strange story about it, but I don't think there are any ghosts.

00:09:52.698 --> 00:09:54.107
What story?

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:56.878
Please tell me," said Jim.

00:09:56.938 --> 00:10:03.360
Well, Mr. Stewart was a very rich, but very strange man.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:08.041
He was very interested in science and experiments.

00:10:08.101 --> 00:10:10.712
He had a lot of enemies.

00:10:10.772 --> 00:10:15.674
People thought his experiments were mysterious and sinister.

00:10:15.734 --> 00:10:19.754
His wife and daughter died in a mysterious accident.

00:10:19.815 --> 00:10:21.632
It was terrible.

00:10:21.692 --> 00:10:25.420
He left San Francisco and returned to New York.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.520
I saw a face grandpa.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:28.461
I did.

00:10:28.521 --> 00:10:29.822
Said Jim.

00:10:29.882 --> 00:10:32.953
But Jim, you don't believe in ghosts?

00:10:33.013 --> 00:10:34.394
Said his grandfather.

00:10:34.454 --> 00:10:35.624
You're right.

00:10:35.684 --> 00:10:37.776
But I saw that girl's face.

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:39.116
Said Jim.

00:10:39.176 --> 00:10:41.537
Maybe it was your imagination.

00:10:41.597 --> 00:10:44.118
Said his grandfather kindly.

00:10:44.178 --> 00:10:47.790
Jim went to his room and turned on the radio.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:52.204
He listened to some songs and then started doing his homework.

00:10:52.264 --> 00:10:56.728
The next day, Jim went to work at the supermarket.

00:10:56.788 --> 00:10:58.199
It was a busy day.

00:10:58.219 --> 00:11:03.624
A strange man with long hair and a silver earring came in.

00:11:03.684 --> 00:11:05.725
His clothes were old.

00:11:05.785 --> 00:11:10.028
Customers were usually friendly, but this man was not.

00:11:10.089 --> 00:11:14.292
He had an angry expression, paid quickly and left.

00:11:14.352 --> 00:11:17.575
It was something strange about him.

00:11:17.635 --> 00:11:21.880
When Jim went home that evening, he phoned Brian.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.214
Hi, how was your day?

00:11:24.274 --> 00:11:25.636
Very busy.

00:11:25.696 --> 00:11:26.816
Said Brian.

00:11:26.876 --> 00:11:28.798
Yes, mine too.

00:11:28.858 --> 00:11:32.761
Do you want to see that new science fiction movie on at the Big Screen Movie Theater?

00:11:32.821 --> 00:11:34.432
We can meet at 7 p.m.

00:11:34.452 --> 00:11:35.413
in front of the park.

00:11:35.473 --> 00:11:36.704
Said Jim.

00:11:36.764 --> 00:11:38.626
Okay, I'll see you then.

00:11:38.686 --> 00:11:39.686
Said Brian.

00:11:39.746 --> 00:11:41.248
At Washington Square.

00:11:41.308 --> 00:11:42.808
Don't be late.

00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:46.352
Jim left the house and started walking to the park.

00:11:46.411 --> 00:11:50.114
He stopped in front of the gate of the old Stuart Mansion again.

00:11:50.174 --> 00:11:52.594
There was no one at the window.

00:11:52.654 --> 00:11:55.053
He stayed there a few minutes.

00:11:55.113 --> 00:11:59.826
It was windy, and the big trees in the garden made strange noises.

00:11:59.886 --> 00:12:01.636
He looked at his watch.

00:12:01.696 --> 00:12:03.908
It was nearly seven o'clock.

00:12:03.968 --> 00:12:07.819
He was late to meet Brian.

00:12:07.879 --> 00:12:11.642
Listening activity.

00:12:11.702 --> 00:12:13.022
One.

00:12:13.082 --> 00:12:14.383
Excuse me.

00:12:14.443 --> 00:12:16.484
What time does the next cable car leave?

00:12:16.544 --> 00:12:21.386
Well, they go every 20 minutes, so the next one will leave at 10 to 11.

00:12:21.446 --> 00:12:24.586
That's in 10 minutes.

00:12:24.646 --> 00:12:27.256
Two.

00:12:27.316 --> 00:12:31.249
Tickets on sale here for a guided tour of Alcatraz.

00:12:31.309 --> 00:12:36.674
Next tour starts in half an hour at a quarter past three.

00:12:36.733 --> 00:12:39.326
Three.

00:12:39.386 --> 00:12:41.277
What time shall we meet?

00:12:41.338 --> 00:12:46.072
Well, I finish work at seven o'clock and Washington Square is very near.

00:12:46.132 --> 00:12:48.113
Let's meet at five past seven.

00:12:48.173 --> 00:12:50.595
Is that okay?

00:12:50.655 --> 00:12:53.122
Four.

00:12:53.182 --> 00:12:55.710
Jim, why are you late for school?

00:12:55.770 --> 00:13:01.660
I'm sorry, sir, but there was a problem with the bus and it didn't leave until 9.30.

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.274
Five.

00:13:04.334 --> 00:13:05.826
Hi, Susan.

00:13:05.886 --> 00:13:07.772
What time are you finishing work today?

00:13:07.832 --> 00:13:15.360
Well, Mrs. Moreno first asked me to work only in the morning and finish at around half past 12 or 20 to 1.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:20.103
But then she asked me to also look after the children during the afternoon as well.

00:13:20.163 --> 00:13:25.887
So I'll finish between half past 5 and quarter to 6.

00:13:25.948 --> 00:13:47.010
Chapter 3 The Stewart Mansion After the movies, the two boys went to eat an ice cream at Pier 39.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.350
It was a beautiful night.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:54.964
They stopped and looked at Alcatraz Island in the middle of San Francisco Bay.

00:13:55.024 --> 00:13:58.646
Jim told Brian about the face at the window.

00:13:58.706 --> 00:13:59.787
What?

00:13:59.847 --> 00:14:01.096
said Brian.

00:14:01.156 --> 00:14:02.564
I don't believe it.

00:14:02.624 --> 00:14:04.434
I want to come with you next week.

00:14:04.494 --> 00:14:06.145
I want to see her too.

00:14:06.205 --> 00:14:07.186
Really?

00:14:07.246 --> 00:14:09.456
That's great," said Jim.

00:14:09.517 --> 00:14:11.268
It's a strange place.

00:14:11.328 --> 00:14:13.498
I'm always a little frayed when I go alone.

00:14:13.558 --> 00:14:15.700
Let's go together soon.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:20.502
On Monday after school, the two friends met Susan at the bus stop.

00:14:20.562 --> 00:14:22.272
They got on the bus.

00:14:22.332 --> 00:14:23.933
Where are you going?

00:14:23.993 --> 00:14:25.264
Susan asked.

00:14:25.324 --> 00:14:27.005
Can you keep a secret?

00:14:27.065 --> 00:14:28.099
asked Jim.

00:14:28.159 --> 00:14:30.124
Why do you have a secret?

00:14:30.184 --> 00:14:31.225
Ask Susan?

00:14:31.285 --> 00:14:33.956
Yes, I do, said Jim.

00:14:34.016 --> 00:14:36.809
Is it about Jenny Lee's new boyfriend?

00:14:36.869 --> 00:14:38.050
Ask Susan.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.382
Jenny was a very popular girl in their class.

00:14:41.442 --> 00:14:45.494
Susan hoped Jenny Lee's new boyfriend wasn't Jim.

00:14:45.555 --> 00:14:50.468
He told her about the Stuart Mansion and about the face of the window.

00:14:50.528 --> 00:14:57.954
Then he told his friends his grandfather's story about the mansion, the scientist and the mysterious accident.

00:14:58.014 --> 00:15:00.866
Scary, said Susan.

00:15:00.926 --> 00:15:03.936
Old mansions always have ghosts.

00:15:03.996 --> 00:15:05.827
Can I come with you?

00:15:05.887 --> 00:15:11.869
Jim smiled at her and said, of course, but promise not to tell anyone.

00:15:11.929 --> 00:15:15.210
Jim was happy that Susan wanted to come.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.880
Susan was pretty.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:20.171
Hey, come on, it's our stop, said Brian.

00:15:20.231 --> 00:15:21.542
Let's get off.

00:15:21.602 --> 00:15:23.912
It was 4.30 p.m.

00:15:23.972 --> 00:15:26.676
and it was a cold sunny afternoon.

00:15:26.736 --> 00:15:30.052
The three friends walked up Telegraph Hill.

00:15:30.113 --> 00:15:35.006
When they arrived at the Stewart Mansion, they stopped in front of the old gate.

00:15:35.066 --> 00:15:37.598
What a strange place!

00:15:37.658 --> 00:15:38.888
said Susan.

00:15:38.948 --> 00:15:41.460
It's cool, said Brian.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:46.504
They looked at the window on the second floor, but they saw nothing.

00:15:46.565 --> 00:15:49.606
They started talking and looking around.

00:15:49.666 --> 00:15:52.949
Hey, do you smell anything strange?

00:15:53.009 --> 00:15:54.300
said Susan.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.061
They stopped and smelled the air.

00:15:57.121 --> 00:16:00.102
It was a very bad smell in the air.

00:16:00.162 --> 00:16:02.154
What is that smell?

00:16:02.214 --> 00:16:03.344
Ask Brian.

00:16:03.404 --> 00:16:04.626
I don't know.

00:16:04.685 --> 00:16:06.737
It smells like rotten eggs.

00:16:06.797 --> 00:16:08.108
Said Jim.

00:16:08.168 --> 00:16:09.760
Yes, that's true.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.641
But where is it coming from?

00:16:11.701 --> 00:16:13.252
Ask Brian.

00:16:13.312 --> 00:16:15.994
Susan and Brian looked at Jim.

00:16:16.055 --> 00:16:19.387
Then they looked at the window on the second floor again.

00:16:19.447 --> 00:16:22.670
Are you sure you saw a face, Jim?

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.300
Ask Susan.

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:26.764
Jim didn't know what to say.

00:16:26.824 --> 00:16:29.456
There was no one at the window now.

00:16:29.516 --> 00:16:34.699
This is a scary place, but I don't see any ghosts, said Brian.

00:16:34.759 --> 00:16:38.341
This smell is terrible, said Susan.

00:16:38.401 --> 00:16:40.752
Let's go home and forget about the ghost.

00:16:40.812 --> 00:16:43.324
It was probably your imagination, Jim.

00:16:43.384 --> 00:16:45.154
Look, cried Jim.

00:16:45.214 --> 00:16:47.466
There's yellow smoke over there.

00:16:47.526 --> 00:16:52.798
Near the bottom window of the mansion, they saw strange yellow smoke in the air.

00:16:52.858 --> 00:16:55.822
Wow, you're right, said Susan.

00:16:55.882 --> 00:16:58.464
What's happening here, said Brian?

00:16:58.524 --> 00:17:01.026
It smells like a dead body.

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:03.648
Maybe there's a dead body in the mansion.

00:17:03.708 --> 00:17:07.330
Maybe this is a secret cemetery, said Jim.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:10.222
Brian's face became white.

00:17:10.282 --> 00:17:12.494
The three friends looked at each other.

00:17:12.514 --> 00:17:15.556
A secret cemetery?

00:17:15.617 --> 00:17:17.327
They said softly.

00:17:17.388 --> 00:17:21.481
They were curious, but terrified at the same time.

00:17:21.541 --> 00:17:23.686
No one knew what to say.

00:17:23.746 --> 00:17:25.790
Oh, please, let's go home.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.691
This place frightens me.

00:17:27.751 --> 00:17:28.931
Said Susan.

00:17:28.991 --> 00:17:31.542
There's something strange happening here.

00:17:31.602 --> 00:17:33.002
Said Brian.

00:17:33.062 --> 00:17:38.234
They agreed to leave and went to Jim's house to listen to his new CDs.

00:17:38.294 --> 00:17:42.075
They sat in Jim's room and talked about the mansion.

00:17:42.135 --> 00:17:48.887
Then Susan suddenly said, Hey, there's the big Chinese New Year parade this Saturday night.

00:17:48.947 --> 00:17:51.317
I'm taking the Moreno children.

00:17:51.377 --> 00:17:52.908
It's always lots of fun.

00:17:52.968 --> 00:17:53.776
Said Jim.

00:17:53.836 --> 00:17:55.064
I'm going to go.

00:17:55.124 --> 00:17:58.918
Me too, said Brian.

00:17:58.978 --> 00:18:03.773
A guide to San Francisco.

00:18:03.833 --> 00:18:11.811
San Francisco is an international center for business, education, science, and the arts.

00:18:11.871 --> 00:18:18.564
Thousands of tourists visit the city every year because there are many interesting places to see.

00:18:18.624 --> 00:18:22.602
San Francisco is a very cosmopolitan city.

00:18:22.662 --> 00:18:25.983
People from all over the world live there.

00:18:26.043 --> 00:18:30.514
There are a lot of multicultural neighborhoods.

00:18:30.574 --> 00:18:37.686
Chinatown is a very big, colorful Chinese neighborhood on Grant Avenue.

00:18:37.746 --> 00:18:40.587
The streets here are narrow.

00:18:40.648 --> 00:18:45.129
There are Chinese food shops, souvenir shops and restaurants.

00:18:45.189 --> 00:18:49.560
There are also Chinese libraries and Chinese schools.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:55.484
Many children from Chinese families go to Chinese school after regular school.

00:18:55.544 --> 00:19:00.806
They want to learn to speak, read and write their parents language.

00:19:00.866 --> 00:19:06.791
The street signs and shop signs in Chinatown are in Chinese too.

00:19:06.851 --> 00:19:12.094
Alcatraz Island is a small island in San Francisco Bay.

00:19:12.154 --> 00:19:18.066
It is a big tourist attraction because it was a famous prison for many years.

00:19:18.126 --> 00:19:22.446
There was one guard or every three to five prisoners.

00:19:22.506 --> 00:19:27.166
Some prisoners tried to escape, but they failed.

00:19:27.226 --> 00:19:35.038
It was impossible to escape from Alcatraz by swimming across to San Francisco because of the cold water.

00:19:35.098 --> 00:19:41.999
Alcatraz was home to many dangerous criminals, like the gangster, Al Capone.

00:19:42.059 --> 00:19:48.762
The prison was closed in 1963 because the conditions were very bad.

00:19:48.822 --> 00:19:51.784
Now, it is a museum.

00:19:51.844 --> 00:19:56.848
You can see photographs of some of the prisoners there and read about them.

00:19:56.908 --> 00:20:02.523
There are many exciting movies about Alcatraz Island and its prisoners.

00:20:02.583 --> 00:20:07.086
Pier 39 is another famous attraction on the bay.

00:20:07.146 --> 00:20:14.522
There are many different shops, games galleries, ice cream stands, and entertainments on the pier.

00:20:14.582 --> 00:20:18.594
Many of the shops sell funny t-shirts.

00:20:18.654 --> 00:20:22.075
Fisherman's Wharf is on the bay too.

00:20:22.135 --> 00:20:27.878
There are hundreds of fishing boats and outdoor food stands with good seafood.

00:20:27.938 --> 00:20:32.119
There are also many street artists and souvenir shops.

00:20:32.179 --> 00:20:37.462
At Fisherman's Wharf, you can take an exciting boat ride on the bay.

00:20:37.522 --> 00:20:43.414
Remember to wear warm clothes because it's sometimes very windy on the bay.

00:20:43.474 --> 00:20:48.842
The cable car is a common form of transportation in San Francisco.

00:20:48.902 --> 00:20:52.420
It climbs up and down the city's hills.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.492
It is great fun to ride the cable car.

00:20:56.552 --> 00:21:01.635
Golden Gate Park is a big park in the middle of the city.

00:21:01.696 --> 00:21:09.020
There are many excellent museums, a famous aquarium, and a flower conservatory.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:14.932
You can also ride your bike or go jogging in this beautiful park.

00:21:14.992 --> 00:21:20.151
A great symbol of San Francisco is the Golden Gate Bridge.

00:21:20.211 --> 00:21:24.802
It is a spectacular bridge with its red orange color.

00:21:24.862 --> 00:21:32.786
It was very difficult to build it in 1937 because of the strong winds and rough sea.

00:21:32.846 --> 00:21:37.258
It connects San Francisco to Northern California.

00:21:37.318 --> 00:21:41.650
Another bridge connects the city to Eastern California.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:45.302
This is called the Bay Bridge.

00:21:45.362 --> 00:21:49.364
Union Square is in the city center.

00:21:49.424 --> 00:21:56.998
It is an international shopping area with many famous designer shops and big department stores.

00:21:57.058 --> 00:22:01.439
There are many tall buildings in the center of San Francisco.

00:22:01.499 --> 00:22:04.530
They are called skyscrapers.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:09.983
One skyscraper looks like a giant triangle.

00:22:10.043 --> 00:22:15.735
The weather in San Francisco is often foggy and windy.

00:22:15.795 --> 00:22:18.216
It doesn't rain a lot.

00:22:18.276 --> 00:22:24.360
A lot of people go to live in San Francisco because it has so many attractions.

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:37.985
The people of San Francisco are very popular in America because they are usually very friendly and outgoing.

00:22:38.045 --> 00:22:54.026
Chapter 4 Chinese New Year This was the Year of the Dragon.

00:22:54.086 --> 00:22:57.538
The Chinese believe that the Dragon brings good luck.

00:22:57.598 --> 00:23:02.148
The Chinese New Year Parade is a very big event in San Francisco.

00:23:02.208 --> 00:23:08.774
It always takes place on a Saturday night between January 21st and February 19th.

00:23:08.834 --> 00:23:11.706
The date depends on the position of the moon.

00:23:11.766 --> 00:23:15.149
Thousands of people go to see the parade every year.

00:23:15.209 --> 00:23:22.784
There are many beautiful costumes, Chinese music, and Grand Avenue is decorated with colorful lanterns.

00:23:22.844 --> 00:23:26.597
A long paper dragon moves along Grand Avenue.

00:23:26.657 --> 00:23:30.110
There are firecrackers and lots of noise.

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:34.304
Jim and Brian took the cable car to Grand Avenue.

00:23:34.364 --> 00:23:37.426
It was always fun to ride the cable car.

00:23:37.486 --> 00:23:40.910
Susan and their high school friends were at the parade.

00:23:40.970 --> 00:23:43.702
Jenny Lee was there with her new boyfriend.

00:23:43.762 --> 00:23:47.656
He was the captain of the football team and he was handsome.

00:23:47.716 --> 00:23:50.436
There was a big crowd everywhere.

00:23:50.496 --> 00:23:57.830
Suddenly, on the other side of the street, Jim saw the face of the little girl at the window in the crowd.

00:23:57.890 --> 00:24:02.654
Jim told Brian, let's follow her, said Brian.

00:24:02.714 --> 00:24:07.598
It was difficult to move because there were lots of people everywhere.

00:24:07.658 --> 00:24:10.820
Then the big paper dragon appeared in the parade.

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:14.604
The little girl suddenly disappeared behind the long dragon.

00:24:14.664 --> 00:24:17.315
How can anyone disappear so quickly?

00:24:17.375 --> 00:24:18.522
Said Jim.

00:24:18.582 --> 00:24:21.269
They went back to watch the parade.

00:24:21.329 --> 00:24:24.960
Maybe she is a ghost, he thought.

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:27.431
The weekend passed quickly.

00:24:27.491 --> 00:24:30.792
It was Monday morning and they were at school.

00:24:30.852 --> 00:24:34.013
Brian and Jim told Susan about the girl.

00:24:34.073 --> 00:24:37.644
Now she wanted to explore the Stuart Mansion too.

00:24:37.704 --> 00:24:40.246
They made plans during lunch.

00:24:40.306 --> 00:24:42.846
Let's go this evening after dinner.

00:24:42.906 --> 00:24:46.188
Remember to bring a flashlight and wear dark clothes.

00:24:46.248 --> 00:24:47.855
Said Jim.

00:24:47.915 --> 00:24:50.522
They were very excited.

00:24:50.582 --> 00:24:54.454
When school finished at 3.15 pm, they ran out.

00:24:54.514 --> 00:24:56.775
They wanted to go home quickly.

00:24:56.835 --> 00:25:02.427
At about 7 pm, they met in front of Jim's house on Telegraph Hill.

00:25:02.487 --> 00:25:06.849
When they arrived at the Stewart Mansion, everything was dark.

00:25:06.909 --> 00:25:09.380
It was a foggy, windy night.

00:25:09.440 --> 00:25:14.152
They looked at the window on the second floor, but there was no one there.

00:25:14.212 --> 00:25:17.963
They climbed over the fence and went into the garden.

00:25:18.023 --> 00:25:21.146
The tall trees moved in the wind.

00:25:21.206 --> 00:25:23.617
I don't smell anything this time.

00:25:23.677 --> 00:25:24.688
Said Susan.

00:25:24.748 --> 00:25:25.829
Me neither.

00:25:25.889 --> 00:25:27.190
Agreed Jim.

00:25:27.250 --> 00:25:28.721
And now what do we do?

00:25:28.781 --> 00:25:30.012
Ask Brian.

00:25:30.072 --> 00:25:31.283
I don't know.

00:25:31.343 --> 00:25:32.604
Said Jim.

00:25:32.664 --> 00:25:34.516
Let's look inside.

00:25:34.576 --> 00:25:36.508
There are windows near the ground.

00:25:36.567 --> 00:25:37.538
Said Susan.

00:25:37.598 --> 00:25:40.571
And let's remember to be very quiet.

00:25:40.631 --> 00:25:41.712
She whispered.

00:25:41.772 --> 00:25:42.632
Okay.

00:25:42.692 --> 00:25:44.247
Said Jim.

00:25:44.307 --> 00:25:48.684
The three friends went to a window and looked inside.

00:25:48.744 --> 00:25:51.388
The glass was old and dirty.

00:25:51.448 --> 00:25:54.441
Brian turned on his flashlight and looked.

00:25:54.501 --> 00:25:58.536
It was a small room with an old desk and some chairs.

00:25:58.596 --> 00:26:01.919
This was probably the study, said Brian.

00:26:01.979 --> 00:26:04.282
Susan turned on her flashlight.

00:26:04.342 --> 00:26:07.446
Look at the newspaper on the desk, said Susan.

00:26:07.506 --> 00:26:11.370
I can't see well, but I think it's yesterday's newspaper.

00:26:11.430 --> 00:26:13.080
Look at the headline.

00:26:13.140 --> 00:26:16.082
Water's scarce in San Francisco.

00:26:16.142 --> 00:26:19.384
But no one lives here, said Jim.

00:26:19.444 --> 00:26:24.786
They looked inside another window and saw a big room with old furniture.

00:26:24.846 --> 00:26:26.898
It looked like the living room.

00:26:26.958 --> 00:26:32.548
On the wall, there was a big painting of a man, a woman, and a little girl.

00:26:32.608 --> 00:26:36.970
Look, that's probably a painting of the Stewart family, said Susan.

00:26:37.030 --> 00:26:40.854
Yes, before the mysterious accident, said Jim.

00:26:40.914 --> 00:26:44.087
And the little girl has long dark hair.

00:26:44.147 --> 00:26:47.840
She looks like the girl at the window, said Susan.

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:51.163
But we saw the little girl at the parade, said Brian.

00:26:51.223 --> 00:26:53.085
How can she be a ghost?

00:26:53.145 --> 00:26:58.423
Remember, she disappeared behind the dragon very quickly, said Jim.

00:26:58.483 --> 00:27:01.328
They went to the other side of the mansion.

00:27:01.348 --> 00:27:04.818
It was a broken window near the bottom of the house.

00:27:04.878 --> 00:27:06.619
They looked inside.

00:27:06.679 --> 00:27:09.300
They saw a big dark basement.

00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:11.040
No one was there.

00:27:11.100 --> 00:27:14.001
Then Jim turned on his flashlight, too.

00:27:14.061 --> 00:27:17.302
In the basement, they saw some long tables.

00:27:17.362 --> 00:27:22.573
There were test tubes, glass bottles, and other laboratory equipment.

00:27:22.633 --> 00:27:26.014
This looks like our chemistry lab, said Jim.

00:27:26.074 --> 00:27:27.995
Maybe someone is using it.

00:27:28.055 --> 00:27:29.066
Said Susan.

00:27:29.126 --> 00:27:30.598
But why?

00:27:30.658 --> 00:27:34.189
Maybe someone is experimenting with something secret.

00:27:34.249 --> 00:27:35.310
Said Brian.

00:27:35.370 --> 00:27:37.450
I don't like this place.

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:38.550
Said Susan.

00:27:38.610 --> 00:27:40.781
It gives me a bad feeling.

00:27:40.841 --> 00:27:41.981
Are you scared?

00:27:42.042 --> 00:27:43.012
Ask Brian.

00:27:43.072 --> 00:27:43.792
No.

00:27:43.852 --> 00:27:46.393
I want to come back again but in the daytime.

00:27:46.453 --> 00:27:47.353
Said Susan.

00:27:47.413 --> 00:27:48.103
Okay.

00:27:48.163 --> 00:27:49.013
Said Jim.

00:27:49.073 --> 00:27:50.594
Let's go then.

00:27:50.654 --> 00:27:51.944
Crash!

00:27:52.004 --> 00:27:53.705
There was a loud noise.

00:27:53.765 --> 00:27:56.165
It came from one of the rooms upstairs.

00:27:56.225 --> 00:27:57.316
What was that?

00:27:57.376 --> 00:27:58.463
Cried Susan.

00:27:58.523 --> 00:28:00.251
We're not alone here.

00:28:00.311 --> 00:28:03.794
Someone or something is here," said Jim.

00:28:03.854 --> 00:28:06.476
Let's get out of here," said Brian.

00:28:06.536 --> 00:28:08.638
They started running to the fence.

00:28:08.698 --> 00:28:14.512
They ran under the trees and suddenly heard a strange sound from the branches above their heads.

00:28:14.572 --> 00:28:15.794
They looked up.

00:28:15.854 --> 00:28:16.414
Eek!

00:28:16.474 --> 00:28:17.494
cried Susan.

00:28:17.554 --> 00:28:18.616
Butts!

00:28:18.676 --> 00:28:26.540
They climbed over the fence quickly and ran away.

00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:44.386
Chapter 5 A Mysterious Magician Jim heard the voice of a child in the fog.

00:28:44.446 --> 00:28:47.640
It was a cold night.

00:28:47.701 --> 00:28:50.403
Jim stood in front of the Stuart mansion.

00:28:50.463 --> 00:28:52.606
There was fog everywhere.

00:28:52.666 --> 00:28:55.588
The voice came from inside the mansion.

00:28:55.648 --> 00:28:57.598
He didn't know what to do.

00:28:57.658 --> 00:29:01.830
He wanted to help the child, but he also wanted to run away.

00:29:01.890 --> 00:29:04.701
Suddenly, he felt a hand on his arm.

00:29:04.761 --> 00:29:06.701
For a moment his heart stopped.

00:29:06.761 --> 00:29:10.062
He could not turn around, he was too scared.

00:29:10.122 --> 00:29:14.254
An angry voice behind him said, What do you want?

00:29:14.314 --> 00:29:16.694
Jim turned around slowly.

00:29:16.754 --> 00:29:21.961
He saw a big man with long dark hair and angry eyes.

00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:25.787
It's the same man I saw at the supermarket two weeks ago.

00:29:25.847 --> 00:29:27.538
He thought.

00:29:27.598 --> 00:29:30.660
He was about 50 years old.

00:29:30.721 --> 00:29:34.023
He had a silver tooth and it shone in the dark.

00:29:34.083 --> 00:29:36.394
He also had a silver earring.

00:29:36.454 --> 00:29:38.136
He was awful.

00:29:38.196 --> 00:29:41.107
Well, what do you want here?

00:29:41.168 --> 00:29:43.937
Jim looked at him and said, Nothing.

00:29:43.997 --> 00:29:45.008
Nothing.

00:29:45.068 --> 00:29:46.278
Who are you?

00:29:46.338 --> 00:29:47.648
Don't ask questions.

00:29:47.708 --> 00:29:49.089
Stay away from here.

00:29:49.149 --> 00:29:50.899
I'm a dangerous man.

00:29:50.959 --> 00:29:54.190
I eliminate problems and you're a problem.

00:29:54.250 --> 00:29:55.300
Go away.

00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:55.911
Now.

00:29:55.971 --> 00:29:59.772
He pushed Jim to the ground and disappeared in the fog.

00:29:59.832 --> 00:30:01.482
Jim woke up.

00:30:01.542 --> 00:30:03.213
He was scared.

00:30:03.273 --> 00:30:04.443
Phew.

00:30:04.503 --> 00:30:07.194
It was only a dream, he thought.

00:30:07.254 --> 00:30:09.334
He looked at his alarm clock.

00:30:09.394 --> 00:30:11.675
It was 3 a.m.

00:30:11.735 --> 00:30:18.558
The next day, Jim, Brian, and Susan went back to the mansion in the afternoon.

00:30:18.618 --> 00:30:20.990
They went to the basement window.

00:30:21.050 --> 00:30:22.620
No one was there.

00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:26.703
But there was a big black book on one of the tables.

00:30:26.763 --> 00:30:29.925
Someone was here last night or this morning.

00:30:29.985 --> 00:30:31.836
There's a book on the table.

00:30:31.896 --> 00:30:33.747
It wasn't here last night.

00:30:33.807 --> 00:30:34.597
Said Jim.

00:30:34.658 --> 00:30:36.932
You're right, said Brian.

00:30:36.992 --> 00:30:39.438
And who has the keys to the mansion?"

00:30:39.498 --> 00:30:40.620
asked Susan.

00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:44.133
That's a good question, said Brian.

00:30:44.193 --> 00:30:48.456
The days passed, and something else happened.

00:30:48.516 --> 00:30:54.032
The grass in Washington Square was green again, and there were flowers.

00:30:54.092 --> 00:30:57.375
Everyone in the neighborhood was surprised and happy.

00:30:57.436 --> 00:31:00.154
Jim talked with his grandfather about this.

00:31:00.214 --> 00:31:02.730
Grandpa, it's amazing.

00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:05.301
Washington Square is beautiful again.

00:31:05.361 --> 00:31:07.781
The grass and the flowers are growing.

00:31:07.841 --> 00:31:09.012
But how?

00:31:09.072 --> 00:31:10.612
There's no rain.

00:31:10.672 --> 00:31:13.492
How can grass and flowers grow without water?

00:31:13.552 --> 00:31:14.603
Said Jim.

00:31:14.663 --> 00:31:15.933
You're right.

00:31:15.993 --> 00:31:17.493
It's strange.

00:31:17.553 --> 00:31:20.534
There's no rain, but the grass is growing.

00:31:20.594 --> 00:31:21.714
Said Grandpa.

00:31:21.774 --> 00:31:25.054
There's an article in today's newspaper about it.

00:31:25.115 --> 00:31:27.046
Jim started reading.

00:31:27.106 --> 00:31:31.048
The grass and flowers are growing again in Washington Square.

00:31:31.108 --> 00:31:35.550
The square was dry for months, but now it is beautiful and green.

00:31:35.610 --> 00:31:42.692
The organizer of the Jazz Festival, Mike Murphy says, I thought it wasn't possible to have the Jazz Festival this year.

00:31:42.752 --> 00:31:45.934
But now it's beautiful and we can have the festival as we always do.

00:31:45.994 --> 00:31:49.536
Artists from all over California are coming this year.

00:31:49.596 --> 00:31:54.571
Some people believe something mysterious is happening in Washington Square.

00:31:54.631 --> 00:32:00.337
One person said, there's no rain, but the grass and the flowers are growing.

00:32:00.397 --> 00:32:04.198
I don't believe in magic, but it's very strange.

00:32:04.259 --> 00:32:06.400
Who is the magician?

00:32:06.460 --> 00:32:16.688
Mr. Magician, can you bring San Francisco some rain too?

00:32:16.748 --> 00:32:36.446
Chapter 6 The Game One afternoon, Susan took the Moreno children to Washington Square.

00:32:36.506 --> 00:32:38.978
They played in the small playground.

00:32:39.038 --> 00:32:41.050
Then they went to the duck pond.

00:32:41.110 --> 00:32:46.024
The children liked feeding the ducks in the pond, but the ducks were not hungry.

00:32:46.084 --> 00:32:49.527
Suzy, why aren't the ducks eating the bread?

00:32:49.587 --> 00:32:51.402
Asked little Sally Moreno.

00:32:51.462 --> 00:32:52.648
I don't know.

00:32:52.708 --> 00:32:53.789
It's strange.

00:32:53.849 --> 00:32:55.650
They're usually hungry.

00:32:55.710 --> 00:32:57.812
The fish aren't hungry either.

00:32:57.872 --> 00:32:58.923
Said Susan.

00:32:58.983 --> 00:33:02.276
Well, it's half past five and it's time to go home.

00:33:02.336 --> 00:33:06.490
The next morning there was a big crowd at Washington Square.

00:33:06.550 --> 00:33:10.202
Jim, Brian, and Susan were there with many other people.

00:33:10.262 --> 00:33:12.944
Everyone was at the duck pond.

00:33:13.004 --> 00:33:16.878
Some of the ducks were dead and others were sick.

00:33:16.938 --> 00:33:19.242
Lots of fish were dead too.

00:33:19.302 --> 00:33:20.954
This is terrible."

00:33:21.014 --> 00:33:21.965
said Susan.

00:33:22.025 --> 00:33:24.606
Someone poisoned those poor ducks.

00:33:24.666 --> 00:33:26.076
Said Jim.

00:33:26.136 --> 00:33:30.408
At that moment, the bus came and the students got on.

00:33:30.468 --> 00:33:34.600
On the bus, everyone continued talking about the ducks.

00:33:34.661 --> 00:33:39.722
Early the next morning, Jim's grandfather bought the newspaper.

00:33:39.782 --> 00:33:43.574
During breakfast, this is what they read.

00:33:43.634 --> 00:33:50.353
Eight ducks and many fish were found dead in the pond in Washington Square yesterday morning.

00:33:50.413 --> 00:33:54.392
Only last week, people came to see the jazz festival.

00:33:54.452 --> 00:33:56.323
It was a great success.

00:33:56.383 --> 00:34:04.188
A scientist analyzed the grass and the water in the pond and found a high quantity of a new chemical.

00:34:04.249 --> 00:34:08.982
The new chemical is similar to greenex, but it is more toxic.

00:34:09.042 --> 00:34:13.146
Greenex was a popular fertilizer 20 years ago.

00:34:13.206 --> 00:34:17.124
It is illegal to use it today, the scientist said.

00:34:17.185 --> 00:34:22.833
The volunteer organization helping hands is now looking after the sick ducks.

00:34:22.893 --> 00:34:26.845
Volunteers can call this number 3920369.

00:34:26.905 --> 00:34:33.387
The San Francisco Police Department are investigating the case.

00:34:33.448 --> 00:34:34.818
Wow!

00:34:34.878 --> 00:34:36.119
Exclaimed gym.

00:34:36.179 --> 00:34:39.920
This mysterious new chemical is responsible for the green grass.

00:34:39.980 --> 00:34:44.178
So someone created a new fertilizer and it's toxic.

00:34:44.238 --> 00:34:48.516
What irresponsible people, said Jim's grandfather.

00:34:48.576 --> 00:34:50.378
Think of the children.

00:34:50.438 --> 00:34:53.610
They play in Washington Square.

00:34:53.670 --> 00:34:57.652
On Thursday evening, Jim and Brian were at Susan's house.

00:34:57.712 --> 00:35:00.673
This fertilizer thing is so strange.

00:35:00.733 --> 00:35:04.236
Maybe it's a mad scientist, said Brian.

00:35:04.296 --> 00:35:08.337
Maybe they can make a lot of money with this new fertilizer, said Jim.

00:35:08.398 --> 00:35:13.042
Yes, a lot of money, and they'll poison all the animals, said Brian.

00:35:13.102 --> 00:35:15.915
Susan was quiet for a few minutes.

00:35:15.975 --> 00:35:19.696
Then she said, I want to solve this mystery.

00:35:19.756 --> 00:35:26.929
I think there's a connection between the Stuart Mansion and this fertilizer, but I don't know.

00:35:26.990 --> 00:35:32.061
On Friday evening, Susan went to see her brother's football game.

00:35:32.121 --> 00:35:36.733
It was San Francisco University versus Monterey University.

00:35:36.793 --> 00:35:38.744
Tom was a good player.

00:35:38.804 --> 00:35:40.885
The stadium was almost full.

00:35:40.945 --> 00:35:44.251
Susan found a good seat to watch the game.

00:35:44.311 --> 00:35:46.898
Susan liked football games.

00:35:46.958 --> 00:35:49.652
She always went to watch her brother play.

00:35:49.712 --> 00:35:53.736
It was a cold night, and she put her hands in her pockets.

00:35:53.797 --> 00:35:55.899
I'm glad I have a warm jacket.

00:35:55.959 --> 00:35:56.960
She thought.

00:35:57.020 --> 00:35:59.053
Then she looked at her watch.

00:35:59.112 --> 00:36:01.325
It was almost half past eight.

00:36:01.385 --> 00:36:03.988
It was time for the big gang to start.

00:36:04.048 --> 00:36:05.734
She was excited.

00:36:05.794 --> 00:36:10.771
Suddenly two people behind her started talking about Washington Square.

00:36:10.831 --> 00:36:15.814
But she could not hear all of their conversation because there was lots of noise.

00:36:15.874 --> 00:36:18.005
She listened carefully.

00:36:18.065 --> 00:36:20.956
Can't test anymore, not now.

00:36:21.016 --> 00:36:22.477
Said one young woman.

00:36:22.537 --> 00:36:23.868
Too dangerous.

00:36:23.928 --> 00:36:25.178
Said the other.

00:36:25.238 --> 00:36:27.820
These people know something.

00:36:27.880 --> 00:36:29.150
Thought Susan.

00:36:29.210 --> 00:36:32.776
She continued listening, but she did not look at them.

00:36:32.836 --> 00:36:36.892
It's illegal, but the experiment almost finished.

00:36:36.952 --> 00:36:38.282
Said one voice.

00:36:38.342 --> 00:36:39.383
All right.

00:36:39.443 --> 00:36:40.783
On Lombard Street.

00:36:40.843 --> 00:36:42.254
Said the other voice.

00:36:42.314 --> 00:36:44.014
Lombard Street.

00:36:44.074 --> 00:36:46.835
The Stewart Mansion is on Lombard Street.

00:36:46.895 --> 00:36:51.596
So there is a connection between the mansion and Washington Square.

00:36:51.656 --> 00:36:53.276
Susan thought.

00:36:53.336 --> 00:36:55.757
Suddenly she understood.

00:36:55.817 --> 00:36:57.858
I must tell Jim and Brian.

00:36:57.918 --> 00:36:58.778
She thought.

00:36:58.838 --> 00:37:02.251
She was very excited and looked at her watch.

00:37:02.311 --> 00:37:07.666
The game finished on time, and San Francisco University won.

00:37:07.726 --> 00:37:10.408
After the game, she phoned Jim.

00:37:10.468 --> 00:37:14.422
She told him about the conversation between the two young women.

00:37:14.482 --> 00:37:16.783
You're a great detective, Susan.

00:37:16.843 --> 00:37:17.754
You're right.

00:37:17.814 --> 00:37:20.736
It's that secret laboratory, said Jim.

00:37:20.796 --> 00:37:23.098
Let's tell the police immediately.

00:37:23.158 --> 00:37:24.058
Said Susan.

00:37:24.118 --> 00:37:26.500
Yes, that's the right thing to do.

00:37:26.560 --> 00:37:28.031
Tomorrow's Saturday.

00:37:28.091 --> 00:37:30.596
Let's meet early in the morning, said Jim.

00:37:30.656 --> 00:37:33.822
I'll call the supermarket and tell them I can't work.

00:37:33.882 --> 00:37:35.494
Okay, said Susan.

00:37:35.554 --> 00:37:37.594
I'll call Brian now.

00:37:37.654 --> 00:37:44.080
It was lucky I went to Tom's football game, she thought.

00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:49.675
Natural resources and pollution.

00:37:49.735 --> 00:37:54.429
Natural resources are the most important things on our planet.

00:37:54.490 --> 00:37:56.882
We cannot live without them.

00:37:56.942 --> 00:38:07.839
There are many kinds of natural resources, light, air, water, soil, plants and wildlife are all natural resources.

00:38:07.899 --> 00:38:11.502
Water is an essential natural resource.

00:38:11.562 --> 00:38:19.562
Water is becoming scarce and many people continue to waste it, especially in Western countries.

00:38:19.622 --> 00:38:23.580
In many countries, people do not have enough.

00:38:23.640 --> 00:38:30.154
Sometimes people die in these countries because they cannot find clean water to drink.

00:38:30.214 --> 00:38:33.766
Air is another essential natural resource.

00:38:33.826 --> 00:38:39.591
Cars, factories and toxic chemicals all create air pollution.

00:38:39.651 --> 00:38:45.764
Pollution damages the quality of our air, especially in big cities.

00:38:45.824 --> 00:38:51.268
This means that some children and adults have problems when they breathe.

00:38:51.328 --> 00:38:57.430
Air pollution also contaminates the rain because of the large quantity of acid.

00:38:57.490 --> 00:39:01.237
Acid rain can destroy forests.

00:39:01.297 --> 00:39:05.184
Our plants and wildlife are in danger too.

00:39:05.244 --> 00:39:08.275
Trees give us the oxygen we breathe.

00:39:08.335 --> 00:39:12.957
But people do not always respect our forests or wildlife.

00:39:13.017 --> 00:39:18.400
People cut down many trees every year to make paper and other things.

00:39:18.460 --> 00:39:22.391
When we use pesticides, they go into the soil.

00:39:22.451 --> 00:39:27.236
This is dangerous because we eat foods from soil.

00:39:27.296 --> 00:39:32.011
Fires can also destroy plants and wildlife.

00:39:32.071 --> 00:39:35.752
Some people are careless and create fires.

00:39:35.812 --> 00:39:39.693
Sometimes these fires burn for several days.

00:39:39.753 --> 00:39:44.444
They destroy trees and kill a lot of animals and birds.

00:39:44.504 --> 00:39:52.956
So, if we want to help conserve our natural resources, we must be careful and look after the environment.

00:39:53.016 --> 00:39:55.912
We must not use too much water.

00:39:55.972 --> 00:40:03.531
When we are outside, we must not drop things in the street or throw things in rivers or in the sea.

00:40:03.592 --> 00:40:17.023
Remember, we can help conserve our natural resources only when we work together.

00:40:17.083 --> 00:40:37.138
Chapter 7 The Police Station On Saturday morning, Jim, Brian and Susan went to Chinatown Police Station.

00:40:37.198 --> 00:40:40.770
Good afternoon, Brian said to the policeman at the door.

00:40:40.830 --> 00:40:42.282
What can I do for you?

00:40:42.342 --> 00:40:43.492
Ask the policeman.

00:40:43.553 --> 00:40:45.194
We want to report something.

00:40:45.254 --> 00:40:46.244
Said Brian.

00:40:46.304 --> 00:40:48.016
Come to my office and sit down.

00:40:48.076 --> 00:40:49.156
Said the policeman.

00:40:49.216 --> 00:40:51.008
I'm Sergeant Chan.

00:40:51.068 --> 00:40:54.290
They explained everything to Sergeant Chan.

00:40:54.350 --> 00:40:57.550
He was interested and a little surprised.

00:40:57.610 --> 00:40:59.728
Why were you at the Stewart Mansion?

00:40:59.788 --> 00:41:01.470
Ask Sergeant Chan.

00:41:01.530 --> 00:41:04.722
One day I saw the face of a little girl at the window.

00:41:04.782 --> 00:41:05.553
Said Jim.

00:41:05.613 --> 00:41:08.185
I told my friends and we wanted to explore it.

00:41:08.245 --> 00:41:11.037
Did you see anyone inside this secret lab?

00:41:11.097 --> 00:41:12.568
Ask Sergeant Chan.

00:41:12.628 --> 00:41:14.270
No, we didn't.

00:41:14.330 --> 00:41:15.360
Said Jim.

00:41:15.420 --> 00:41:16.581
I understand.

00:41:16.641 --> 00:41:18.182
Said Sergeant Chan.

00:41:18.243 --> 00:41:21.294
The mansion is very close to Washington Square.

00:41:21.354 --> 00:41:24.307
Perhaps you discovered something interesting that night.

00:41:24.367 --> 00:41:27.107
I'll send some officers to investigate.

00:41:27.167 --> 00:41:29.466
I want you to come, too.

00:41:29.526 --> 00:41:32.319
You know where the laboratory is.

00:41:32.380 --> 00:41:33.760
I'll phone you.

00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:34.851
Yes, Sergeant.

00:41:34.911 --> 00:41:36.522
Answer, Jim.

00:41:36.582 --> 00:41:40.646
In the afternoon, the phone rang at Jim's house.

00:41:40.706 --> 00:41:41.727
Hello.

00:41:41.787 --> 00:41:45.030
This is Sergeant Chan of the San Francisco Police Department.

00:41:45.090 --> 00:41:46.952
May I speak to Jim Riley?

00:41:47.012 --> 00:41:48.263
This is Jim Riley.

00:41:48.323 --> 00:41:49.820
Hello, Sergeant Chan.

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:54.130
Jim, my officers and I are going to investigate the Stuart Mansion.

00:41:54.190 --> 00:41:56.712
Can we meet you at five o'clock this afternoon?

00:41:56.772 --> 00:41:57.712
Of course!

00:41:57.772 --> 00:42:01.586
Let's meet in front of my house at 325 Lombard Street.

00:42:01.646 --> 00:42:03.257
Then we can go together.

00:42:03.317 --> 00:42:07.090
Said Jim, you and your friends wait outside your house.

00:42:07.150 --> 00:42:08.712
We'll go in a police car.

00:42:08.772 --> 00:42:10.263
Said Sergeant Chan.

00:42:10.323 --> 00:42:12.315
We'll see you at five o'clock then.

00:42:12.375 --> 00:42:13.656
Goodbye.

00:42:13.716 --> 00:42:15.368
Jim was excited.

00:42:15.428 --> 00:42:18.314
He told his grandfather about the phone call.

00:42:18.375 --> 00:42:21.210
I'm very proud of you and your friends.

00:42:21.270 --> 00:42:25.052
You're doing the right thing," said his grandfather.

00:42:25.112 --> 00:42:28.214
He smiled, but he was worried.

00:42:28.274 --> 00:42:30.124
Thanks, Grandpa.

00:42:30.185 --> 00:42:32.786
Jim called Brian and Susan.

00:42:32.846 --> 00:42:34.757
Meet me outside my house.

00:42:34.817 --> 00:42:37.608
The police are going to drive us to the mansion.

00:42:37.668 --> 00:42:39.819
It was 5 p.m.

00:42:39.880 --> 00:42:43.071
Jim saw two police cars in front of his house.

00:42:43.131 --> 00:42:46.770
He and his friends got into the police car with Sergeant Chan.

00:42:46.830 --> 00:42:47.706
Good evening.

00:42:47.766 --> 00:42:49.288
This is Sergeant Lopez.

00:42:49.348 --> 00:42:50.399
Said Sergeant Chan.

00:42:50.439 --> 00:42:51.580
Please immediately, sir.

00:42:51.600 --> 00:42:52.330
Please immediately, sir.

00:42:52.390 --> 00:42:54.412
Said Jim Bryan and Susan.

00:42:54.472 --> 00:42:56.484
Now this is our plan.

00:42:56.544 --> 00:43:01.016
We'll drive to the mansion, and my officers and I will go in.

00:43:01.076 --> 00:43:04.580
Jim, you will show us the basement window.

00:43:04.640 --> 00:43:07.952
After that, you must stay outside the mansion.

00:43:08.012 --> 00:43:11.487
Only the police will enter, because it can be dangerous.

00:43:11.548 --> 00:43:12.950
Do you understand?

00:43:13.010 --> 00:43:14.362
Yes, I do, sir.

00:43:14.422 --> 00:43:18.034
I'll wait outside with my friends," said Jim.

00:43:18.094 --> 00:43:21.527
The police car drove up Telegraph Hill.

00:43:21.587 --> 00:43:28.512
When they arrived in front of the Stewart Mansion, Jim, Sergeant Chan, and Sergeant Lopez got out of the car.

00:43:28.572 --> 00:43:31.574
Three policemen got out of the second car.

00:43:31.634 --> 00:43:34.346
The five men followed Jim.

00:43:34.406 --> 00:43:37.028
He took them to the gate.

00:43:37.088 --> 00:43:39.841
The policemen looked around.

00:43:39.901 --> 00:43:46.446
You go around the back of the house, and we'll go around the front," said Sergeant Chan to the other policeman.

00:43:46.506 --> 00:43:48.888
Where did you see this laboratory?

00:43:48.948 --> 00:43:50.539
Sergeant Chan asked Jim.

00:43:50.599 --> 00:43:53.852
Over there, by the window replied Jim.

00:43:53.912 --> 00:43:57.394
They saw yellow smoke near the basement window.

00:43:57.454 --> 00:43:59.996
It was a bad smell like before.

00:44:00.056 --> 00:44:03.318
That's the smell of sulfur, said Sergeant Chan.

00:44:03.378 --> 00:44:05.310
And it's very strong.

00:44:05.370 --> 00:44:07.842
He opened the gate and went in.

00:44:07.902 --> 00:44:10.302
The other policeman followed him.

00:44:10.362 --> 00:44:18.396
Jim remained outside with his friends and waited.

00:44:18.456 --> 00:44:37.739
Chapter 8 The Secret Formula There were four young people in the laboratory, two women and two men.

00:44:37.799 --> 00:44:42.443
They were in their early twenties and they were very busy with an experiment.

00:44:42.503 --> 00:44:45.286
They stood around the long table.

00:44:45.346 --> 00:44:48.508
One woman wrote something in the big black book.

00:44:48.569 --> 00:44:51.311
The other three worked with the test tubes.

00:44:51.331 --> 00:44:55.494
It was a portable computer on a small desk.

00:44:55.554 --> 00:44:58.708
Near the desk, there was a little girl.

00:44:58.768 --> 00:45:04.382
The little girl was with the man with long hair and a silver earring.

00:45:04.442 --> 00:45:10.265
Sergeant Chan looked inside the basement window and saw people in the laboratory.

00:45:10.325 --> 00:45:12.076
Jim Riley was right.

00:45:12.136 --> 00:45:14.377
There is an illegal laboratory here.

00:45:14.437 --> 00:45:17.589
Let's go in, said Sergeant Chan to his men.

00:45:17.649 --> 00:45:21.231
The police broke the front door and went into the mansion.

00:45:21.291 --> 00:45:23.644
They immediately went to the basement.

00:45:23.704 --> 00:45:26.397
This is the San Francisco Police Department.

00:45:26.457 --> 00:45:27.967
Put your hands over your heads!

00:45:28.027 --> 00:45:29.678
Sergeant Lopez cried.

00:45:29.738 --> 00:45:31.409
You have the right to remain silent.

00:45:31.469 --> 00:45:33.580
Anything you say can be used against you.

00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:36.440
The young people were surprised and angry.

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:37.581
Oh no!

00:45:37.641 --> 00:45:39.302
cried one young man.

00:45:39.362 --> 00:45:43.133
He and his friend ran to another door, but the police stopped them.

00:45:43.193 --> 00:45:45.654
Who are you and what are you doing here?

00:45:45.714 --> 00:45:47.895
Do you know you're on private property?

00:45:47.955 --> 00:45:49.746
said Sergeant Chan.

00:45:49.806 --> 00:45:51.946
One of the young women spoke.

00:45:52.006 --> 00:45:53.878
She was very nervous.

00:45:53.938 --> 00:45:56.261
My name is Barbara Dell.

00:45:56.321 --> 00:45:58.271
We aren't criminals.

00:45:58.331 --> 00:46:03.083
We're students at San Francisco University in the Department of Chemistry.

00:46:03.143 --> 00:46:04.203
Who is that man?

00:46:04.263 --> 00:46:05.804
He doesn't look like a student.

00:46:05.864 --> 00:46:07.444
Said Sergeant Chan.

00:46:07.504 --> 00:46:09.214
He's Ben Bradley.

00:46:09.274 --> 00:46:14.966
He has the key to the mansion because his grandfather was a gardener here many years ago.

00:46:15.026 --> 00:46:17.497
Now Ben doesn't have a home.

00:46:17.557 --> 00:46:19.128
He sleeps here at night.

00:46:19.188 --> 00:46:20.828
Said Barbara Dell.

00:46:20.888 --> 00:46:22.367
Aw, shut up!

00:46:22.427 --> 00:46:24.618
said Ben Bradley angrily.

00:46:24.678 --> 00:46:27.488
Be quiet, said Sergeant Chan.

00:46:27.548 --> 00:46:29.439
Now continue your story.

00:46:29.499 --> 00:46:31.299
Don't tell them anything, Barbara.

00:46:31.359 --> 00:46:32.920
Cried one of the young men.

00:46:32.980 --> 00:46:35.110
The formula is our secret.

00:46:35.170 --> 00:46:36.721
I want to tell the truth.

00:46:36.781 --> 00:46:37.991
Said Barbara.

00:46:38.051 --> 00:46:41.561
We discovered a new molecule at the university.

00:46:41.621 --> 00:46:46.973
With this molecule, we created a new formula for a powerful fertilizer.

00:46:47.033 --> 00:46:50.525
People can use this fertilizer without water.

00:46:50.585 --> 00:46:53.416
We knew that no one lived in this mansion.

00:46:53.476 --> 00:46:59.380
And we knew that there was an old laboratory in the basement because Mr. Stewart was a scientist.

00:46:59.440 --> 00:47:02.131
We wanted to keep this a secret because...

00:47:02.191 --> 00:47:05.513
Because you wanted to sell it to a company and make a lot of money.

00:47:05.573 --> 00:47:08.876
And you tested the fertilizer in Washington Square.

00:47:08.937 --> 00:47:11.558
You polluted the water of the duck pond.

00:47:11.618 --> 00:47:14.049
You killed the ducks and the fish.

00:47:14.109 --> 00:47:18.050
Your new fertilizer is toxic and very dangerous.

00:47:18.110 --> 00:47:21.381
Do you know the children play in the park near the duck pond?

00:47:21.441 --> 00:47:23.672
Ask Sergeant Chen angrily.

00:47:23.732 --> 00:47:27.422
We didn't want to pollute the water in the pond or the grass in the park.

00:47:27.482 --> 00:47:29.013
Said one of the young men.

00:47:29.073 --> 00:47:31.634
We just wanted to test the new fertilizer.

00:47:31.694 --> 00:47:34.804
And you decided to test it in a public park.

00:47:34.864 --> 00:47:38.040
Didn't you think about the people and the wildlife?

00:47:38.100 --> 00:47:42.528
You four must come with us to the police station, said Sergeant Chan.

00:47:42.588 --> 00:47:46.660
We will also take all the chemicals you're using in this laboratory.

00:47:46.721 --> 00:47:51.724
The little girl at the desk was scared and started crying.

00:47:51.784 --> 00:47:54.716
She ran to Barbara Dell.

00:47:54.776 --> 00:47:55.616
Who is she?

00:47:55.676 --> 00:47:57.257
asked Sergeant Lopez.

00:47:57.317 --> 00:47:58.788
She's my little sister.

00:47:58.848 --> 00:48:00.439
I bring her here sometimes.

00:48:00.499 --> 00:48:02.009
Said Barbara.

00:48:02.069 --> 00:48:07.960
Then the policeman, the university students, and Ben Bradley came out of the mansion.

00:48:08.020 --> 00:48:11.260
Jim, Brian, and Susan were outside.

00:48:11.321 --> 00:48:15.222
When Jim saw Ben Bradley, he was very surprised.

00:48:15.282 --> 00:48:18.603
It's the man from the supermarket, he thought.

00:48:18.663 --> 00:48:21.124
The little girl looked at Jim.

00:48:21.184 --> 00:48:23.254
Well, she's not a ghost.

00:48:23.314 --> 00:48:24.175
She's real.

00:48:24.235 --> 00:48:25.522
He thought.

00:48:25.582 --> 00:48:31.644
Sergeant Chan smiled at Jim, Brian, and Susan and said, You helped us a lot.

00:48:31.704 --> 00:48:32.804
Thank you.

00:48:32.864 --> 00:48:36.967
Come to the police station tomorrow, and I'll explain everything.

00:48:37.028 --> 00:48:38.758
Thank you again.

00:48:38.818 --> 00:48:42.090
The police cars drove away.

00:48:42.150 --> 00:48:46.934
The next day, the three friends went to talk to Sergeant Chan.

00:48:46.994 --> 00:48:50.936
Those university students were very intelligent, said Jim.

00:48:50.996 --> 00:48:53.030
They created a new formula.

00:48:53.090 --> 00:48:56.282
Yes, but they were also very irresponsible.

00:48:56.342 --> 00:48:59.754
We found many illegal chemicals in that basement.

00:48:59.814 --> 00:49:02.586
Those chemicals are very toxic.

00:49:02.647 --> 00:49:06.188
Now we must close Washington Square for a few weeks.

00:49:06.248 --> 00:49:10.811
There will be a lot of work for our chemical experts, Sid Sergeant Chan.

00:49:10.871 --> 00:49:13.843
What will happen to the university students?

00:49:13.903 --> 00:49:15.003
Ask Susan.

00:49:15.063 --> 00:49:17.995
There will be a trial, Sid Sergeant Chan.

00:49:18.055 --> 00:49:19.739
They could go to prison.

00:49:19.799 --> 00:49:21.252
How are the other ducks?"

00:49:21.312 --> 00:49:22.443
asked Brian.

00:49:22.503 --> 00:49:25.504
The volunteers at helping hands are looking after them.

00:49:25.564 --> 00:49:26.825
They're feeling better.

00:49:26.885 --> 00:49:28.786
Said Sergeant Chan.

00:49:28.846 --> 00:49:32.257
Jim, Brian, and Susan left the police station.

00:49:32.317 --> 00:49:34.098
They were all happy.

00:49:34.158 --> 00:49:36.048
Pizza for everyone tonight.

00:49:36.108 --> 00:49:37.038
Said Jim.

00:49:37.098 --> 00:49:38.229
Great idea.

00:49:38.289 --> 00:49:39.269
Said Brian.

00:49:39.329 --> 00:49:42.521
Let's go to Nico's pizza place on Washington Square.

00:49:42.581 --> 00:49:43.801
Said Susan.

00:49:43.861 --> 00:49:46.202
Jim and Brian looked worried.

00:49:46.262 --> 00:49:49.012
Don't worry, I'm only joking.

00:49:49.072 --> 00:49:50.263
Said Susan laughing.

